{
  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The residual is plausible but its scale is unspecified relative to SASRec’s normalized features and embedding scaling. Consequently, alpha values 0.1 and 0.3 may have very different effects across implementations. Padding masks, next-item alignment, dropout, and checkpoint configuration need explicit definitions.",
    "A recent-window residual can improve ranking through short-term item co-occurrence without improving order-sensitive reasoning. Include a last-item residual and an order-invariant history-pooling control before attributing gains to repeated recent interests. Originality 3 is reasonable; potential 7 and difficulty 2 remain provisional without baseline implementation details or measurements.",
    "The diagnostic adapter remains underspecified: define measured rank-based metrics, sample counts, missing-value handling, deterministic sampling, and restoration of model mode. Separately document the required full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty training users. Training margins cannot substantiate claims about compatibility or current intent.",
    "The experiment needs a budgeted schedule, checkpoint-selection rule, and a statement of whether alpha is shared across all four datasets. Report per-category results alongside the macro average and paired uncertainty; repeatedly selecting configurations on the same 800 validation users risks adaptive overfitting."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify residual scaling and establish whether the implementation is reproducible across SASRec variants.",
      "query": "In the original SASRec paper and official implementation, how are item embeddings scaled, layer normalization applied, padding masked, and next-item targets aligned? When adding a causal mean of recent item embeddings to the final sequence features, what normalization and dropout choices preserve a meaningful residual coefficient?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Check overlooked prior art and identify controls that distinguish recent co-occurrence from sequence reasoning.",
      "query": "How do FPMC, FOSSIL, and SASRec combine long-term user preferences with recent-item or Markov signals? What ablations distinguish gains from last-item transitions, recent-window embedding pooling, repeated interests, and order-sensitive encoding in sequential recommendation?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make validation selection and diagnostic claims defensible within the fixed search budget.",
      "query": "For sequential recommendation evaluated with one positive and 99 fixed sampled negatives per user, what methods address adaptive validation overfitting and estimate paired uncertainty when comparing hyperparameters? Consider four equally weighted datasets, 200 validation users each, a fixed training seed, and checkpoint selection under a limited GPU budget."
    }
  ]
}
